BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>Black holes: flight in a Kerr spacetime</h1>
A black hole of 10^5 solar masses, spin 0.9, alone. A delta-glider on a
circular orbit at 10 masses goes round at 0.31 c: its radius held, its
period and its clock's rate against the Kerr spacetime's. Another hovers
on the spin axis on the ideal drive, at 677,000 g: held in place, its
clock slowed by gravity. A third falls from rest through the horizon
and is lost at the inner horizon.
END_HYPERDESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System BlackHoleTest
  Date MJD 51982.6685767396
  Script Tests/BlackHoleTest
END_ENVIRONMENT

BEGIN_FOCUS
  Ship ORB
END_FOCUS

BEGIN_CAMERA
  TARGET ORB
  MODE Extern
  POS 4 0 -20
  TRACKMODE TargetRelative
  FOV 50.00
END_CAMERA

BEGIN_SHIPS
ORB:DeltaGlider
  STATUS Orbiting TestHole
  ELEMENTS 1.0e12 0.00000 0.0 0.0 0.0 0.0 51982.6685767396
  AROT 0 0 0
END
HOV:DeltaGlider
  STATUS Orbiting TestHole
  ELEMENTS 1.1e12 0.00000 0.0 0.0 0.0 120.0 51982.6685767396
  AROT 0 0 0
END
FALL:DeltaGlider
  STATUS Orbiting TestHole
  ELEMENTS 1.2e12 0.00000 0.0 0.0 0.0 240.0 51982.6685767396
  AROT 0 0 0
END
END_SHIPS
